1. First: What the Agent Pattern Represents
The diagram you shared describes a three‑zone multi‑agent architecture:
Zone 1 — Constitution
• The “source of truth”
• Rules, policies, constraints
• Transparency + governance
Zone 2 — Runtime Inference Pipeline
• Acting Agent (classify, extract, validate, reason)
• Critic Agent (evaluate, approve/reject)
• ALF (human simulator)
• Final output
Zone 3 — Learning & Evolution Loop
• Exception feedback
• Rule Learning Agent
• SME review
• Updating the Constitution
This is a closed-loop, self-improving agent system.

